@@END
#ASSERT `offence under s 408` `an employee`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 408` `a breach of trust`

#ASSERT (`charge under s 406` `a breach of trust`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of June 2026, at about 9.00 pm, at Blk 1 Toa Payoh Lorong 1, Singapore, being entrusted with property, namely, a sum of $5,000, did dishonestly misappropriate the said sum, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 406 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 406` `illus (d), the agent in good faith`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 406 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal breach of trust (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: dishonestly misappropriates or converts to his own use that property, or dishonestly uses or disposes of that property in violation of a direction of law or a legal contract, or intentionally suffers any other person to do so."

