§ `Cheating - ss 415-420A`

-- The reference row's s 420 case, Lewis Christine v Public Prosecutor [2001] SGHC 113
@@FIX `Lewis Christine` : Cheating Facts
=particulars => Particulars WITH accused IS "Christine Lewis", date IS "the 24th day of April 2000", time IS "8.10 pm", place IS "the Seiyu Departmental Store at Parkway Parade Shopping Centre", `co-accused` IS "", `common intention` IS FALSE
=victim => "Wong Fei Hsia"
=victim described as => "the cashier of Seiyu Departmental Store"
=victim pronoun => she
deceived the victim
=the deception => "to believe that the price of a \"Pochacco\" pencil casing is worth $5.25, when in actual fact, you knew that the price of the said item is worth $16.95"
dishonestly
deliver
=the property => "the said item for only $5.25"
@@END
#ASSERT cheats `Lewis Christine`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 420(1)` `Lewis Christine`)'s text EQUALS "You, Christine Lewis, are charged that you, on or about the 24th day of April 2000, at about 8.10 pm, at the Seiyu Departmental Store at Parkway Parade Shopping Centre, Singapore, did cheat one Wong Fei Hsia, the cashier of Seiyu Departmental Store by deceiving her to believe that the price of a \"Pochacco\" pencil casing is worth $5.25, when in actual fact, you knew that the price of the said item is worth $16.95, and by such manner of deception, you dishonestly induced the said Wong Fei Hsia to deliver to you the said item for only $5.25 which she would not have done, had she not been so deceived, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 420 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT `offence under s 417` `Lewis Christine`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 420(2)` `Lewis Christine`

-- fraudulently only: s 417 stands, s 420 withdraws
@@FIX `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only` : Cheating Facts < `Lewis Christine`
-dishonestly
fraudulently
@@END
#ASSERT `offence under s 417` `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 420(1)` `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 420(1)` `Lewis Christine, fraudulently only`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 420 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of cheating and dishonestly inducing a delivery of property (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: dishonestly (section 420 requires dishonesty; fraud alone is section 417)."

-- s 415 illus (a)-(f), (h), (i): each a deception that dishonestly induced a delivery - A cheats
#ASSERT cheats `Lewis Christine`
-- s 415 illus (g): A meant to deliver the pepper when he took the money - no deception, no cheating
@@FIX `illus (g), the pepper honestly promised` : Cheating Facts < `Lewis Christine`
-deceived the victim
@@END
#ASSERT NOT cheats `illus (g), the pepper honestly promised`
-- s 415 illus (k): the automated ticketing system - the company is deceived though no officer is (Explanations 4, 5)
#ASSERT cheats `Lewis Christine`
-- the second limb: an act induced intentionally, causing harm in property
@@FIX `the second limb` : Cheating Facts
deceived the victim
intentionally
do
causes
harm
property
@@END
#ASSERT cheats `the second limb`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 420(1)` `the second limb`

-- s 416 illus (a): pretending to be a rich banker of the same name - cheating by personation
@@FIX `s 416 illus (a), the banker` : Cheating Facts < `Lewis Christine`
pretending to be some other person
@@END
#ASSERT `cheats by personation` `s 416 illus (a), the banker`
#ASSERT `offence under s 419` `s 416 illus (a), the banker`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 419` `Lewis Christine`

-- s 416B, s 420(2): a scam call
@@FIX `a scam call` : Cheating Facts < `Lewis Christine`
the deception is conducted mainly by way of remote communication
@@END
#ASSERT `cheats by remote communication` `a scam call`
#ASSERT `offence under s 420(2)` `a scam call`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 420(2)` `a scam call`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years and with caning with not less than 6 strokes, and shall also be liable to fine"
@@FIX `a call on an excluded system` : Cheating Facts < `a scam call`
a system or method the Minister
@@END
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 420(2)` `a call on an excluded system`

-- s 418
@@FIX `a trustee cheats` : Cheating Facts < `Lewis Christine`
with the knowledge that he is likely
whose interest
@@END
#ASSERT `offence under s 418` `a trustee cheats`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 418` `Lewis Christine`

-- s 416A
@@FIX `personal information sold` : Personal Information Facts
personal information about another person
knowing or having reason to believe
supplies, offers
knew or had reason to believe it will
@@END
#ASSERT `offence under s 416A` `personal information sold`
@@FIX `personal information kept, no offence in view` : Personal Information Facts
personal information about another person
knowing or having reason to believe
obtains or retains
@@END
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 416A` `personal information kept, no offence in view`
